    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d906">

                <pb facs="1413" n="1399" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1399"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 P.W./12–944</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Atcheson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3213</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-09">December 9,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received December 28.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the Embassy’s
                    despatch No. 3091, October 24, 1944,<anchor n="33" xml:id="d906-f1"/> in regard
                    to the Far Eastern and Pacific Sub-commission of the United Nations War Crimes
                    Commission, and to report that an organizing meeting of the Sub-commission was
                    held at Chungking on November 28, 1944. Copies of the minutes of the meeting
                    have not yet been received; there is accordingly enclosed a brief memorandum
                    describing the action taken, together with copies of pertinent documents which
                    were distributed to the representatives at the meeting.<anchor n="34"
                        xml:id="d906-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>It will be noted that Dr. Wang Chung-hui was elected Chairman of the
                    Sub-commission; that Dr. P. H. Chang, Counselor of the Executive Yuan, was
                    elected Secretary General; that the British, Dutch and American representatives
                    were designated to form a Committee on Financial Arrangements; and that the
                    question of the date on which the war is considered to have begun in China,
                    raised by the Dutch and the Australians, is being referred to the Commission in
                        London.<anchor n="35" xml:id="d906-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">George Atcheson, Jr.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d906-f1" n="33" xml:id="d906-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d906-f2" n="34" xml:id="d906-f2-content">
